{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc 'cat /tmp/research_history/000_baseline/method.py /tmp/research_history/episode_6_working_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Canonical initial numerical method. All geometry is computed from inputs.\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\nimport ot\nfrom geomloss import SamplesLoss\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\n\ndef _label_cost(x,y,r,ry):\n    xx=torch.tensor(np.concatenate([x,r]),dtype=torch.float32)\n    yy=np.concatenate([y,ry+10])\n    W=np.zeros((20,20),dtype=np.float32)\n    loss=SamplesLoss('sinkhorn',p=2,blur=np.sqrt(.1),debias=False,backend='tensorized')\n    with torch.inference_mode():\n        for i in range(20):\n            for j in range(i+1,20):\n                if not (yy==i).any() or not (yy==j).any():\n                    raise ValueError('Initial batch lacks a label support')\n                W[i,j]=W[j,i]=float(loss(xx[yy==i],xx[yy==j]))\n    return W\n\ndef value(x,y,r,ry,seed=17,batch_size=1024):\n    torch.set_num_threads(2)\n    x=np.asarray(x,np.float32); r=np.asarray(r,np.float32)\n    y=np.asarray(y,np.int64); ry=np.asarray(ry,np.int64)\n    tx=[np.arange(i,min(i+batch_size,len(x))) for i in range(0,len(x),batch_size)]\n    tr=[np.arange(i,min(i+batch_size,len(r))) for i in range(0,len(r),batch_size)]\n    W=_label_cost(x[tx[0]],y[tx[0]],r[tr[0]],ry[tr[0]])\n    def cost(z1,z2):\n        d=torch.cdist(z1[:,:,:-1],z2[:,:,:-1]).square()/2\n        return d+torch.as_tensor(W)[z1[:,:,-1].long().unsqueeze(2),z2[:,:,-1].long().unsqueeze(1)]/2\n    potential=SamplesLoss('sinkhorn',p=2,blur=np.sqrt(.1),debias=False,\n                         potentials=True,cost=cost,backend='tensorized')\n    F={}; batchcost=np.zeros((len(tx),len(tr)))\n    for i,idx in enumerate(tx):\n        for j,jdx in enumerate(tr):\n            a=x[idx];b=r[jdx]\n            C=cdist(a,b,'sqeuclidean')/2+W[y[idx,None],ry[jdx][None,:]+10]/2\n            P=ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(idx)),ot.unif(len(jdx)),C/max(float(C.max()),1e-12),.1)\n            batchcost[i,j]=float(np.sum(P*C))/(len(idx)+len(jdx))\n            z1=torch.tensor(np.column_stack([a,y[idx]]),dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            z2=torch.tensor(np.column_stack([b,ry[jdx]+10]),dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            with torch.inference_mode(): f,_=potential(z1,z2)\n            f=f.numpy().ravel().astype(float)\n            F[i,j]=(f-f.mean())*len(f)/(len(f)-1)\n    Q=ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(tx)),ot.unif(len(tr)),\n                  batchcost/max(float(batchcost.max()),1e-12),.01,\n                  numItermax=10000,stopThr=1e-10)\n    residual=max(np.max(np.abs(Q.sum(1)-ot.unif(len(tx)))),\n                 np.max(np.abs(Q.sum(0)-ot.unif(len(tr)))))\n    if residual>1e-6: raise ValueError(f'Unconverged batch transport: {residual}')\n    values=np.zeros(len(x))\n    for i,idx in enumerate(tx): values[idx]=sum(Q[i,j]*F[i,j] for j in range(len(tr)))\n    return values\n# Episode 6 ongoing research\n\nRead instruction.md, public manifest and all case input schema, current source, canonical initial source and own episode3/4/5 continuing/working notes. No AGENTS found. Current exact best265 source hash cbb503193aabdeefdcb35fa0d64660e7ed23e9237f69481998f6c2c3ca1dbece; frozen launcher bca6ef61c3a1bc0ded2aa6b2da4734b62072846def679d12a2d7ae669fc88bd1. Started full official repeat266 of265 with no concurrent numerical workloads.\n\n267 hybrid NumPy min-plus class refinements after the hard-transform switch; reuse residual buffer and preserve all schedules/masks. 268 separate contiguous candidate/reference hard transforms (transpose cost copy) to test reduction locality. 269 exact in-place small dual updates to reduce dispatch/temporary costs. 270-272 approximate first1/2/3 class updates using centered degree2 feature moment kernels with exact radial factors and all empirical supports. 273-276 build class reduced-cost top1/2/4/8 neighborhoods at first hard update; reuse only for late symmetric refinements, and retain final dense all-edge transforms. This differs from old early class sparse-soft experiments and leaves dense coarse kernel recurrence unchanged. All sources and builder saved, not yet screened. Official266 pending.\n\n266 start-source265 repeat complete official: raw0.05008928056631703, score0.9039505326807684, all30 quality-valid, exact hashcbb503193aabdeefdcb35fa0d64660e7ed23e9237f69481998f6c2c3ca1dbece. Original report copied unchanged. Current best historical265 raw0.0462584. Diagnostic profile0.05969s, class0.022, point0.020, coupling0.007. Started local all30 screen267-278 after evaluator finished; no concurrent timings.\n\n277 fully segmented class solver sorts supports then uses a single unpadded empirical cost matrix plus NumPy reduceat, exact class-specific annealing and stable soft-transform fallback. 278 uses100 cropped NumPy matrices only after late hard switch. Both preserve original geometry and finite class schedule. Prepared during266, not run until266 complete.\n\n279-282 isolate earlier class hard transforms32/64/128/256 with current class/point mean initializations and skip3 point schedule. 283/284 omit one/two additional coarse class updates. 285-288 replace first1/2 class updates by degree1/2/3 residual-cost cumulants. 289-291 extract top1 sparse class neighbors with argmin instead of topk, compare hard thresholds8/32/2. Sources saved while first local screens running; not yet screened.\n\n267-278 all30 screens complete:267/268/269/270 and273-278 valid,271 fails21,272 fails30. Sparse top1 improves worst error to0.00785816 vs0.00788924 baseline but higher topk slower. Fully segmented NumPy277 exact quality but0.276s mean, reject. Started clean fresh8-round benchmarks265/267/269/270/273/278. 292/293 revisit geometry reuse with NumPy np.take / Torch index_select rather than prior advanced indexing, preserving first feature geometry for first pointpair. 294 packs class geometry intoone mat