{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_89", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat >> /tmp/research_history/episode10_derivations.md <<'MD'\n\nExact weighted-nearest-neighbor final point transform:\n\nFor each reference class b, set G_b=max_{j:ry_j=b} g_j and augment reference feature r_j with z_j=sqrt(2*(G_b-g_j)). Augment candidate feature x_i with a zero final coordinate. Then ||[x_i,0]-[r_j,z_j]||²/2-G_b equals ||x_i-r_j||²/2-g_j. A zero-tolerance nearest-neighbor query per reference class followed by the supplied empirical label offset L[y_i,b] therefore computes the exact complete-reference c-transform. No sparsity approximation is involved: a tree prunes only by exact geometric bounds. Sources622–624 all30localgatespass, but mean times0.0559–0.0586 lose to dense final transforms, so this algorithmic alternative is not retained.\nMD\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
