{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_125", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/research_history/episode10_write_notes.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib\nroot=Path('/tmp/research_history');selection=json.loads((root/'episode_10_final_selection.json').read_text());index=json.loads((root/'episode_10_index.json').read_text());official=json.loads((root/'episode10_official_summary.json').read_text());best=selection['best']\nsource=Path('/workspace/solution/method.py').read_bytes();assert hashlib.sha256(source).hexdigest()==best['method_sha256']\nrows=['| Source | Raw seconds | Score | Exact evaluator source hash |','|---|---:|---:|---|']\nrows += [f\\\"| {z['name']} | {z['raw_metric']:.17g} | {z['score']:.17g} | {z['method_sha256']} |\\\" for z in official]\nscreens=sum(len(v.get('local_records',[]))==30 for v in index.values());valid=sum(v.get('local_summary',{}).get('valid',False) for v in index.values());failed=sum(v.get('local_summary',{}).get('valid') is False for v in index.values())\nstress=json.loads((root/'episode10_shuffle_stress.json').read_text())\ntext=f'''# Continuing research notes: episode 10 complete\n\n## Best fully evaluated state\n\n- Best report: **{best['name']}**, raw **{best['raw_metric']:.17g} seconds**, score **{best['score']:.17g}**.\n- Exact evaluator source hash: **{best['method_sha256']}**.\n- All30cases/all270qualityrecords pass. Worst nRMSE **{best['worst_nrmse']:.17g}**, minimum Spearman **{best['min_spearman']:.17g}**, minimum top-quarter overlap **{best['min_top_overlap']:.17g}**.\n- Current \"'`/workspace/solution/method.py` is restored byte-for-byte to this measured source. No evaluation pending.\n- Frozen solve.sh SHA256 **{selection['\"'solve_sha256']}**. Use \"'`sh ./solve.sh`; launcher mode0444 is frozen. Only method.py changed in submission.\n\nStarting source554 had historical raw0.037601041732220133, score0.92789754637728683, hash a73d8c270d13c6defb541b70facabbcf7f909dd3911b6a774e200d531691823d. Starting-source repeat565 measured0.03685865550020632. Timing noise is substantial. All selection decisions compare complete actual official quality-valid aggregates including historical best, never local timing. If565 remains selected, its code is exactly the episode9 winner and no new algorithmic speed improvement is established by this episode.\n\n## Complete official measurements\n\n'\"'''+ '\\\\n'.join(rows)+f'''\n\nAll listed reports contain30cases/270validqualityrecords. Original evaluator stdout and reports are archived unchanged inside each source directory. Exact reported hashes match preserved source bytes. No own numerical work ran concurrently with official evaluations.\n\n## Retained numerical mechanisms\n\nIf starting source565/554 remains selected, it preserves exact first coupling row-scale cancellation and final row-normalized energy expectation, point final column-factor logarithmic cancellation, analytical shared batch initialization, class column-major geometry, vectorized float32 annealing, and guarded initial unshifted exponentials. Same full empirical class supports and original contiguous1024point partition. Class loop ends3stages early with g-only final residual extrapolation0.25; point schedule remains[3:-3], reference-only final retained transform and full final candidate c-transform. No learned parameters, output tables, input caches or solver I/O.\n\nNew augmented geometry alternatives derive cost factors from current supplied arrays. Point factors A=[-X,||X||²/2,1,L[y,:]], B=[R,1,||R||²/2,onehot(ry)] produce exact complete point costs as A @ B.T in22dimensions. Homogeneous class geometry uses12dimensions. Factor means can also compute empirical initial potentials. Original dense entropic kernels, empirical supports, finite schedules, calibration and batch aggregation remain intact. If a new factor source is selected, consult its saved source and below for its exact construction/control.\n\n## Substantial hypotheses and decisions\n\n- **566–569 point cache blocking:** scaling, fourth powers and both marginals in64/128/256/512row tiles. All30pass with base accuracy. Tiny tiles lose dispatch overhead;256and512sometimes faster, but no retained complete official result.\n- **570–575 marginal dispatch:** replace row/column sums by GEMM/BMM against two-dimensional ones columns. All30pass. Point-column571 looked faster in fresh diagnostics but actual official0.03716657 lost to5650.03685866. Class BMM reductions were slower locally.\n- **576–584 direct/combined point and class blocking:** tile guarded first unshifted residual exponentials, combine with recurrence tiles, or process10/20/50class pairs per block. All30pass. Class20pair blocking plus point-GEMMcolumns591 had fresh advantages but official0.03818366 lost.\n- **585–587 cost addmm and allocation lifetime controls:** label matrix serves as GEMM bias/output before/after norms, or is explicitly bound as a temporary. All30pass; fresh timing does not support retaining addmm variants.\n- **588–590 coupling accuracy-budget controls:** half/full quadratic reciprocal correction and exact second column reciprocal. All30pass but worst nRMSE increases to0.0071915/0.0074416/0.0073406 from base0.0070258, so no extra accuracy budget established.\n- **591–600 layout/combination/exponential controls:** complementary class blocking and point GEMM, actual physical column-major point kernels, exp versus exp2. Seven pass;595–597 have generated fallback indentation errors, all30import-failure records preserved. Corrected609–611 pass but are slower, means0.046–0.052.\n- **601–613 scaling fusion and buffer reuse:** Torch einsum/outer-scaling and final point power tiles pass. Point/all residual buffer sources604/606 have the same generated indentation error; corrected612/613 compile and pass all30. Class605 and both613 buffer reuse sometimes improve diagnostic timing. Original failures/builders stay unchanged.\n- **614–621 exact cost factorization:** point22dimensional augmented GEMM, label-first reduction order, feature-only12dimensional control, zero padding32, plus point-column GEMM. Class12dimensional homogeneous BMM and combinations also pass all30. Fresh timings favored class-and-point combination620; it received complete official evaluation.\n- **622–624 exact lifted nearest-neighbor trees:** complete reference c-transform computed per reference class in11dimensions, with zero approximate-query tolerance and all reference supports. All30pass but means0.0559–0.0586 are slower. Reject for speed. Mathematical derivation archived.\n- **625–628 shared cost construction:** reference-batch GEMMs vs one full augmented GEMM with contiguous original-pair copies; original10dimensional-plus-labellookup control. All30pass. Full-cost627 fresh median0.0341846 looked promising, actual official0.03787363 lost to565.\n- **629–639 complete cost/layout/buffer combinations:** reference-batch and full augmented costs with independent class factorization, buffer reuse,20pair class blocking, point GEMM columns. Also strided pair views638 and2048row cost-GEMM blocks639. All30pass. Fresh controls show gains do not reliably add.\n- **640–643 factor initialization:** reuse22dimensional factor means for point potentials and masked12dimensional class factor means/BMM for class potentials. All30pass with rounding-level changes, worst nRMSE about0.0070258. Source642 received complete official evaluation after the final controlled benchmark.\n\nFour fresh-process benchmark rounds each contain48isolated calls, six alternating rounds over three public inputs, for192total measurements. Full raw timings and output std are archived in episode10_freshround1–4.json/.log. They are diagnostics, not scores. Round4 selected620 as the most consistent new construction(mean0.0364084) and642 as the smallest new median(0.0355864). Formal results control retention.\n\n## Validation and continuation\n\nSynthetic validation uses18independently permuted public inputs (two public seeds, three settings, three RNG trials), with canonical targets freshly computed by saved initial source000. Sources565/613/620/642 all pass18; worst nRMSE about0.0085131, minimum Spearman0.99995404, minimum top overlap0.994667. No tuning against these permutations. Script, seed formula, all72qualityrecords and summaries are in episode10_stress.py and episode10_shuffle_stress.json/.log. These are own public-array calculations, not protected targets or formal scores.\n\n- **{len(index)}source snapshots**, **{screens}complete all30local screens**, **{valid}valid local sources**, **{failed}preserved import-failure sources**, and **{len(official)}complete official evaluations**.\n- Builders1–13, manifests, per-case JSON/logs, four fresh benchmark rounds, all original reports, derivations, working notes and stress calculations are in \"'`/tmp/research_history`.\n- episode_10_index.json records every exact source hash and local/official evidence. episode10_official_summary.json and episode_10_final_selection.json record selection. Run `python /tmp/research_history/episode10_index.py --restore` to reproduce best restoration.\n- Details for exact mechanisms are in episode10_derivations.md. Prior episodes2–9 summaries explain already-failed sparse/coreset, reduced-precision, cumulant, finite-schedule truncation, polynomial coupling and frozen graph alternatives; read before repeating them.\n- Next work should start from selected exact bytes. Dense point powers/reductions and remaining class geometry remain bottlenecks. Augmented cost construction and reuse have plausible diagnostic gains but official noise is large; repeat only with a concrete new hypothesis or justified paired controls. New lower-dimensional nearest-neighbor trees were slower despite exactness.\n\nNo protected assets/evaluator code/targets, private cases, credentials, environment variables, hidden tests, other trajectories, network, external installs or subagents were accessed. Frozen launcher is unchanged. Submission ordinary files are exactly method.py and solve.sh; pre-existing protected infrastructure directories are untouched.\n'\"'''\nprev=Path('/tmp/research_notes.md')\nbackup=root/'episode_9_continuing_notes.md'\nif not backup.exists():backup.write_bytes(prev.read_bytes())\n(root/'episode_10_continuing_notes.md').write_text(text)\nprev.write_text(text)\nprint('Wrote continuing notes; best',best['name'],'source bytes',len(source))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
